<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iksan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Geummajeo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iksan is a city in North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeolla-province">Jeolla Province</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>. In the Baekje period it was known as Geummajeo and was an important royal centre, with the great Buddhist temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mireuksa">Mireuksa</a>. After the fall of Goguryeo, Silla settled the refugee prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anseung">Anseung</a> and his followers there in 670, creating the short-lived state of Bodeok.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iksan.jpg" alt="Iksan" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iksanirish · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iksan_-_Young_Deung_Dong.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
